    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d65">

                <pb facs="0081" n="69" xml:id="pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/674a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-12T20:00:00-04:00">December 12, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6308. Department’s 6291, December 11, midnight. The Soviet Ambassador<anchor
                        n="52" xml:id="d65-f1"/> has proposed the following amendment to the joint
                    declaration: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“After the sentence concerning the deliberate extermination of Jews by
                            way of mass executions add: ‘The number of victims of these sanguinary
                            punishments is taken to amount to many hundreds of thousands of quite
                            innocent men, women and children’.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>This amendment is entirely satisfactory to the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d65-f1" n="52" xml:id="d65-f1-content">
                <p>Maxim Maximovich Litvinov.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
